From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panthor: raise the simple_ondemand thresholds

The GPU counts as busy from the moment a job is queued until a scheduler
tick finds every group idle, with a tick every 10 ms and an idle hysteresis
of 800 us. At 144 Hz this reads as busy most of the time, and with an
upthreshold of 45 the GPU goes to its fastest OPP for anything that moves
on the screen.

On the Lenovo TB375FC, a light page scrolling in a browser keeps the GPU at
1400 MHz. The power parts of the GPU rail are audible at the high OPPs.

Raise the thresholds, so the OPP settles lower. A load above the
upthreshold still goes straight to the fastest OPP. The values are not
final, this trades frames on light pages for less power and noise.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
@@ -241,10 +241,12 @@ int panthor_devfreq_init(struct panthor_device *ptdev)
 
 	/*
 	 * Setup default thresholds for the simple_ondemand governor.
-	 * The values are chosen based on experiments.
+	 * The GPU counts as busy from the moment a job is queued until a
+	 * scheduler tick finds every group idle, which is much more than the
+	 * time it works: leave room for that.
 	 */
-	pdevfreq->gov_data.upthreshold = 45;
-	pdevfreq->gov_data.downdifferential = 5;
+	pdevfreq->gov_data.upthreshold = 85;
+	pdevfreq->gov_data.downdifferential = 10;
 
 	pdevfreq->devfreq = devm_devfreq_add_device(dev, &panthor_devfreq_profile,
 						    DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND,
